WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.179 --> 00:00:05.100
Thanksgiving is different now.
It's an old thing. It's as old as America

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:09.599
and older than that. George Washington
did a Thanksgiving Proclamation.

00:00:09.599 --> 00:00:15.139
Lincoln did a famous one 100 years later.

00:00:15.139 --> 00:00:19.619
Traditionally it descends from the
harvest festival which is a seasonal

00:00:19.619 --> 00:00:23.640
thing.
So you spend the summer

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:28.560
getting in the crops, praying for rain or
less rain, it's never the farmers think

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:33.660
it's never the right amount of rain.
And then you have the hectic thing of

00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:37.140
getting the crops in, which is night and
day labor and exhausting, and then you've

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:41.219
got the crops, and that's something to
celebrate.

00:00:41.219 --> 00:00:46.739
Life doesn't work that way anymore.
It isn't seasonal,

00:00:46.739 --> 00:00:51.059
in the same way.
So I think we have to make an effort to

00:00:51.059 --> 00:00:54.600
make it seasonal,
and there's many ways to do that. The

00:00:54.600 --> 00:01:00.539
College is actually in the business of
recalling things that are beyond time.

00:01:00.539 --> 00:01:05.519
Things that are not just seasonal, things
that are eternal because you know at the

00:01:05.519 --> 00:01:08.960
end of the season, Thanksgiving is when
you think about

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:13.340
gratitude to the eternal for the fact
that you've got food to eat,

00:01:13.340 --> 00:01:16.740
and for the chance to do the labor to
produce it.

00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:21.180
We can get the cooperation from nature
that it takes to produce it.

00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:26.759
And we're grateful for that and there's
a natural time to stop and be grateful. I

00:01:26.759 --> 00:01:30.479
think music is a great and powerful way
to go about that.

00:01:30.479 --> 00:01:35.939
Music is a big thing here. I sit in here
here in our Chapel, it's being prepared

00:01:35.939 --> 00:01:40.020
right now for a Christmas video that
you'll have access to pretty soon

00:01:40.020 --> 00:01:44.400
by our new Sacred Music choir. I think
you're going to see that they're

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:48.659
wonderful.
What is the music that they sing?

00:01:48.659 --> 00:01:54.420
It's about the eternal, and music has an
unusual power to transport.

00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:58.799
And Plato's Republic along with
gymnastic, which is things you do to your

00:01:58.799 --> 00:02:05.520
body, to make it better, it is the most
powerful of two powerful things.

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:11.099
Music in Plato’s Republic includes
literature and poetry and all forms of

00:02:11.099 --> 00:02:17.040
art that can affect the mind and the
senses and the emotions,

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:25.860
and so, music is very important.
This morning I started listening to one

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:29.520
of my favorite pieces of music—Fauré's
Requiem.

00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:33.959
It's 35 minutes long. It's very
beautiful.

00:02:33.959 --> 00:02:38.760
The third movement is called Sanctus and
that comes from “sacred” and that word

00:02:38.760 --> 00:02:43.680
“sacred” has meant the same thing in Latin
and all the other languages where it

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:47.819
appears. It means “touching.” They're
connected to the Divine. The holiday

00:02:47.819 --> 00:02:51.300
season, which begins and includes
Thanksgiving and runs through the

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:56.519
wonderful thing of Christmas,
is a great time to celebrate the eternal.

00:02:56.519 --> 00:03:00.959
We have to remember to stop and do that
because

00:03:00.959 --> 00:03:08.280
if we don't remember the eternal, our
temporal work, our work in time, won't be

00:03:08.280 --> 00:03:13.260
meaningful or well directed. Our College
is in the business of remembering the

00:03:13.260 --> 00:03:17.159
sublime
because that is the end of life, and the

00:03:17.159 --> 00:03:22.319
only guide to life that will work.
In this troubled time, and it's very

00:03:22.319 --> 00:03:26.519
troubled, I worry about these times a
great deal,

00:03:26.519 --> 00:03:31.440
and then I remember the Sanctus, and I
remember that sooner or later, all will

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:36.080
be well.
Happy Thanksgiving.

